REALROM sample.warn f35f [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank state becomes unknown here: call to bank-switch helper FUN_f34b, which takes NO INBOUND ARGUMENT -- its own prologue redefines the register its mechanism reads, so there is no caller value to recover. The bank is supplied inside the helper (typically from a RAM shadow) and is not resolved here.
REALROM sample.note f1f1 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call re-commits the bank READ BACK at f1ef from write-through bank shadow 005e -- a RAM cell the switch code keeps in step with every bank it commits, so the byte read is the last bank committed through it -- the save/restore idiom. The bank after this call is whatever 005e held at that read, not a fresh value this analyzer failed to pin down. A property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
REALROM sample.note f335 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is this helper's ARGUMENT: the backward scan reached the helper's entry, where the register holds whatever the caller supplied, so the bank cannot be known from inside the helper body. Each CALL SITE is resolved separately; see the call sites' own annotations.
REALROM sample.note f345 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is this helper's ARGUMENT: the backward scan reached the helper's entry, where the register holds whatever the caller supplied, so the bank cannot be known from inside the helper body. Each CALL SITE is resolved separately; see the call sites' own annotations.
REALROM sample.note f522 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call re-commits the bank READ BACK at f518 from write-through bank shadow 005e -- a RAM cell the switch code keeps in step with every bank it commits, so the byte read is the last bank committed through it, carried on the stack across the call at f51d -- the save/restore idiom. The bank after this call is whatever 005e held at that read, not a fresh value this analyzer failed to pin down. That read sits at the ENTRY of FUN_f516 (nothing switches between its entry and the read), so it is the shadow as the caller left it: each of its call sites' own bank, which those sites already track -- the call passes it through unchanged. A property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
